viralOS root filesystem
=========================

The build assembles this tree from several places in the source code and
packs it into a tar archive (initrd.tar); the bootloader loads that into
memory and the kernel unpacks it into a RAM filesystem (ramfs) at boot.

  rootfs/            hand-written files: /etc, /home, the app launchers, this README
  resources/         the desktop's fonts, icons, sounds...  -> /usr/share/dde-res
  user/programs/     C sources, compiled into /usr/bin
  abi/paths.h        where everything is (the kernel and programs use it)
  scripts/mkinitrd.py  the folder layout and permission rules

Layout (the usual Unix one; names are case-sensitive)
  /dev            disks and partitions ("usb0", "usb0p1"), null, log
  /etc            system settings
                    hostname    the machine's name (shown in the shell prompt)
                    init        the first program to start (the login screen)
                    motd        the message printed after boot
                    os-release  the system's name and version
                    passwd      the accounts: name:x:uid:gid:Display Name:home:shell
                    shadow      their password hashes (PBKDF2-SHA256), "" for none
                    group       a group for each account
                    fstab       where drives get mounted (Disks > Edit Mount Options)
                    network.conf  network adapters' settings (netctl, Settings > Network)
                    dde/settings.conf  the desktop's default settings
  /home/NAME      each user's files: Desktop, Documents, Downloads, Music, Pictures, and
                  .config/dde/ (their own desktop settings: wallpaper, pinned apps, picture...)
  /media          where USB sticks and other drives get mounted
  /root           root's home (root can't log in)
  /tmp            scratch space
  /usr/bin        programs (one per user/programs/*.c or folder, and the ported Linux tools)
  /usr/lib        shared libraries (lib*.so) the programs use
  /usr/share/applications  app launchers, one .desktop file per app:
                    [Desktop Entry]
                    Type=Application
                    Name=File Manager
                    Comment=Manage files on your computer.
                    Icon=/usr/share/dde-res/Icons/Apps/Files.png
                    Exec=/usr/bin/divine-files
  /usr/share/dde-res  DDE's look and feel
                    Backgrounds/  wallpapers; default.png is the default
                    Cursors/      mouse pointers
                    Fonts/        TrueType fonts (DejaVu Sans, Bold, Mono)
                    Icons/        Apps/ (AppsMenu.png: the panel's apps button), Dialogs/,
                                  FilesFolders/ (files, folders, drives), Misc/, Settings/, Status/
                    Sounds/       system sounds

Everything is writable, but nothing is saved back to the ISO.
